From d1f2a73bc41b94f487bc5d8103539ea524d67dd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yohan <you@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:57:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Batch 6: forensic report API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- GET /api/v1/emails/:emailId/report now returns a full print-friendly
  structured report built from stored EmailRecord data (case info,
  evidence integrity, email metadata, authentication, header forensics,
  threat assessment, IOCs, URL/domain analysis, infrastructure/geoloc,
  ML/AI assessment, why-flagged, recommended actions (reuses Batch 5C),
  related-campaign info (reuses Batch 5B), and the two required
  limitation strings) — no PDF generation; frontend uses browser print
- reportBuilder.ts: pure projection, never re-runs parsers/ML/LLM/GeoIP/
  DNS, marks each section UNAVAILABLE/NOT_APPLICABLE rather than
  fabricating content when its source data is missing
- 404 EMAIL_NOT_FOUND preserved for nonexistent emailId
- updated two pre-Batch-6 placeholder tests (scan.test.ts,
  scan-batch5.test.ts) that asserted the old 'not implemented yet' 404,
  since that behavior is now intentionally replaced
- 19 new tests (reportBuilder.test.ts, emails-report.test.ts),
  230/230 passing
- npm run build clean
